title: Countdown
golf: 40

Write `countdown(n)` that returns a list counting down from n to 1.
`countdown(3)` gives `[3, 2, 1]`.
=== starter
def countdown(n):
    ...
=== broken
def countdown(n):
    return list(range(n, 0))
=== test
from harness import eq


def test_countdown(sol):
    eq(sol.countdown(3), [3, 2, 1], "countdown(3)")
    eq(sol.countdown(1), [1], "countdown(1)")
